you'd be forgiven for forgetting about  passengers but jennifer lawrence never  will  if you can't recall passengers is a  sci-fi movie focusing on lawrence and  chris brad's characters  aurora lane and jim preston they are two  passengers among many on an interstellar  journey  and aurora and jim wake up early 90  years  too early as a matter of fact with no  obvious way to go back to sleep  when you have 90 years to kill with  someone things are likely to turn  romantic  out of sheer boredom if nothing else  however even though lawrence and pratt  have strong on-screen chemistry  the act of filming those steamy scenes  was decidedly flaccid  especially for lawrence the actress  recently opened up about the many  ways in which her experience getting  intimate with her co-star was less than  ideal  through no real fault of prats that  doesn't mean she despised filming  passengers  instead whenever she had to get all  lovey-dovey in the film  things turned awkward quickly during a  round table discussion hosted by the  hollywood reporter  jennifer lawrence revealed that  passengers had her first  intimate scene ever on film and she used  liquid courage to help her get through  lawrence said she felt extremely awkward  knowing the scenes she had to film  so to prepare for her big moment she  drank  a lot all that alcohol had unintended  consequences though  lawrence grappled with extreme anxiety  in between  shoots while lawrence knew that her job  was to kiss the then married to anna  fairest chris pratt  even the feigned infidelity gave her a  queasy feeling every time the two had  the lock lips in front of the cameras  to make matters worse the actual process  of filming romantic scenes was less than  fun  one scene that was cut from the film  required pratt and lawrence to rock a  table back and forth  and neither of them liked it when asked  about the scene lawrence said  sex scenes are the most unsexy things in  the world  i can't think of anything else to try  to save us  i don't even want to think about it  anymore the duo's on-screen romance  also led to some real world problems  when acting in a romantic movie there is  always the unspoken fear that fiction  will bleed  over into reality complicating real-life  relationships  when two stars have blazing on-screen  chemistry it is a law of the universe  that the rumor mill is going to kick  into overdrive just ask bradley cooper  and lady gaga  while many celebrities understand that  this is part of the job and can find the  mental fortitude to rise above it  this gossip almost always takes a  psychological toll  tales of behind-the-scenes infidelity  spread like wildfire  after chris pratt and his wife actress  anna faris  announced their divorce jennifer  lawrence was at the top of the list of  potential causes  due unfairly to the romantic scenes she  had filmed with pratt during passengers  lawrence shot those rumors down during  an interview with instyle  stating that the film had already been  wrapped for years by the time  ferris and pratt announced their divorce  not even on a fair spot into the rumors  in her memoir unqualified ferris states  that she was good friends with jennifer  lawrence and was embarrassed by the  gossip faris also writes that lawrence  was apologetic  about the whole thing as she knew it was  adding even more stress onto ferris  during a stressful time  while jennifer lawrence has mostly  unpleasant memories of filming  passengers romance scenes  it wasn't all bad in true jennifer  lawrence style  she liked them the most when they went  off the rails generating some of the  best moments on the film  set during an interview with lawrence  usa today  discovered that one of passengers  funniest moments was completely  unintentional in the movie  lawrence and pratt's characters  eventually don space suits and  after they take the helmets off they go  in for a kiss  but bump into each other because the  suits are so big  that wasn't supposed to happen they were  supposed to lock lips passionately but  the unforeseen  bulky nature of the spacesuits  transformed the scene  into a comedic bit everyone on set liked  it so much that it was left  in the film's final cut this unscripted  moment is yet  another entry and the list of movie  bloopers that were deemed superior to  the intended versions  coincidentally another recent example of  such a scene  also involves chris pratt that time he  accidentally dropped an  infinity stone in guardians of the  galaxy  oops check out one of our newest videos  right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite stars are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

